\[\frac{1+\cos 4\cdot 2\varphi }{\sin 4\cdot 2\varphi } = \frac{\cos 4\varphi + \cos 4(2\varphi - 4\varphi )}{\sin 4\varphi \cos 4\varphi },\]where $\varphi = 1^\circ.$ This is the well-known half angle identity of cotangent. Dividing by $\sin 80^\circ$ and integrating over $\varphi = 1 \text{ to } 44,$\[2\left( \cot 45^\circ + \cot 41^\circ - \cot 4^\circ \right) = \frac{1}{\sin 8^\circ} + \dots + \frac{1}{\sin 40^\circ}.\]This yields an answer of $\boxed{80}.$
